('Technology','MEDIUM','Which company created the first commercially successful handheld electronic game, Auto Race?','Mattel','Mattel Electronics released Auto Race in 1976.'),
('Technology','EASY','What does the USB acronym stand for?','Universal Serial Bus','USB stands for Universal Serial Bus, a standard for connections and data transfer.'),
('Technology','MEDIUM','Which programming language was named after a comedy group?','Python','Guido van Rossum named Python after Monty Python''s Flying Circus.'),
('Technology','EASY','What was the first feature-length film made entirely with computer-generated imagery?','Toy Story','Pixar''s Toy Story premiered in 1995 as the first fully computer-animated feature film.'),
('Technology','MEDIUM','Which company originally developed the Java programming language?','Sun Microsystems','Java was developed at Sun Microsystems and first released publicly in 1995.'),
('Technology','EASY','What does the QR in QR code stand for?','Quick Response','QR means Quick Response, reflecting the code''s intended fast scanning.'),
